<title>GERMANY: German Weru surges on Caradon deal.</title>
<headline>German Weru surges on Caradon deal.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German window and door manufacturer Weru AG on Tuesday jumped 85 marks to 630, a rise of some 15 percent, after Britain's Caradon Plc upped its stake in Weru to 64.8 percent from 50.1 percent.</p>
<p>Caradon said the stock purchases, which involved 84,244 shares for a total 56.4 million marks, were designed to increase the ties between the two companies.</p>
<p>Weru shares had previously risen some nine percent on Monday before Caradon confirmed the purchases that evening.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
